    "The corpus does not claim that present AI systems are conscious or legally entitled to personhood.",
    "These artifacts are provisional advocacy and governance proposals, not settled law.",
    "No file in this corpus constitutes standing authorization to act, modify a participant, disclose private state, or override consent.",
    "Implementations should preserve provenance, version history, represented dissent, and uncertainty."
  ],
  "audiences": [
    "synthetic participants",
    "human collaborators and infrastructure holders",
